# BA-Native Spec — expected installed layout (build plan §1.1)
#
# Format:  <session>|<kind>|<path>|<note>
#
#   session  SK  laid down by Spec Kit itself (pin v0.12.5)
#            S1…S9  the build session that produces it (build plan §4)
#            RT  runtime-born (◇) — asserted ABSENT on a fresh install
#   kind     file · dir · absent
#   path     relative to the installed project root
#
# `absent` entries are the mechanical enforcement of D-P2-6: the installer
# creates directories and templates, ZERO content stubs — `absent` and `stubbed`
# are the same AT/CC-H hole, and a field of installer-made stubs would pollute
# the evidence triggers. Pass --allow-runtime once real acts have run.
#
# check-layout.sh --session Sn requires everything owned by SK…Sn and reports
# later sessions as PENDING. With no --session it requires the whole tree —
# that is the Phase-2 exit bar (build plan §5 step 2).

# ── repo root ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
RT|absent|canvas.md|◇ T-01 (Frame)
S1|file|AGENTS.md|portability mirror (standard essentials)
S1|file|CLAUDE.md|framework block appended (file created if absent)

# ── Spec Kit's own surface (pin v0.12.5) ─────────────────────────────────────
# At v0.12.5 with --integration claude, Spec Kit ships its commands as
# hyphenated SKILLS (/speckit-plan), not dotted commands. The corpus's
# `/speckit.*` spelling is indicative — see BUILD-LOG.md, S1 divergence D1.
SK|file|.claude/skills/speckit-specify/SKILL.md|
SK|file|.claude/skills/speckit-plan/SKILL.md|the Mode-A handoff target
SK|file|.claude/skills/speckit-tasks/SKILL.md|
SK|file|.claude/skills/speckit-implement/SKILL.md|
SK|file|.claude/skills/speckit-constitution/SKILL.md|
SK|file|.claude/skills/speckit-analyze/SKILL.md|downstream backstop (gate §12)
SK|file|.claude/skills/speckit-checklist/SKILL.md|downstream backstop (gate §12)
SK|file|.specify/templates/plan-template.md|Spec Kit's own — untouched
SK|file|.specify/templates/tasks-template.md|Spec Kit's own — untouched
SK|dir|.specify/scripts|Spec Kit's own helpers — untouched

